From: Gemini <gemini@antigravity.internal>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:58:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] arm64: dts: ipq5018-cr8818: configure dual-conduit CPU ports for NSS offload

On the Xiaomi CR8808 Ver.B (CR8818, board profile ap-mp03.3), the physical Ethernet
topology wires the Motorcomm YT9215SC switch to two SoC MACs:
- MAC0 (dp1 / eth0): Connected via Qualcomm Internal GE PHY (0x004dd0c0 at 88000.mdio:07)
  to Switch Port 4 (cpu2).
- MAC1 (dp2 / eth1): Connected via Uniphy SerDes SGMII 1000M to Switch Port 8 (cpu1).
- Physical WAN RJ45: Connected to Switch Port 3.
- Physical LAN1-3 RJ45: Connected to Switch Ports 0, 1, 2.

This patch defines both CPU conduits in the device tree:
1. Enables dp1 (eth0) as dedicated conduit for Port 4 (cpu2), allowing untagged WAN
   forwarding directly into Qualcomm NSS offload.
2. Configures dp2 (eth1) for Port 8 (cpu1) for LAN traffic.
3. Sets up nss_region (8 MiB at 0x40000000) and coherent_pool memory parameters.

Signed-off-by: Gemini <gemini@antigravity.internal>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018-cr8818.dts | 52 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 49 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018-cr8818.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018-cr8818.dts
@@ -18,6 +18,13 @@
 	chosen {
 		bootargs-append = " coherent_pool=512k";
 	};
+
+	reserved-memory {
+		nss_region: nss@40000000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x40000000 0x0 0x800000>; /* Exactly 8 MiB */
+			no-map;
+		};
+	};
 };
 
 &mdio {
@@ -35,6 +42,21 @@
 	};
 };
 
+/* GMAC0: Secondary CPU Conduit (eth0 / cpu2) via Internal GE PHY */
+&dp1 {
+	status = "okay";
+	phy-mode = "internal";
+	phy-handle = <&ge_phy>;
+};
+
+/* GMAC1: Primary CPU Conduit (eth1 / cpu1) via Uniphy SerDes SGMII 1000M */
+&dp2 {
+	status = "okay";
+	phy-mode = "sgmii";
+	phy-handle = <&switch_port8>;
+	qcom,uniphy-serdes = <&uniphy0>;
+};
+
 &switch {
 	ports {
 		#address-cells = <1>;
@@ -60,11 +82,23 @@
 			label = "wan";
 		};
 
+		/* Secondary CPU Conduit: Port 4 (Internal GE PHY / eth0) */
 		port@4 {
 			reg = <4>;
-			status = "disabled";
+			label = "cpu2";
+			ethernet = <&dp1>;
+			phy-mode = "internal";
+			status = "okay";
 		};
 
+		/* Primary CPU Conduit: Port 8 (Uniphy SerDes SGMII / eth1) */
 		port@8 {
 			reg = <8>;
-			label = "cpu";
+			label = "cpu1";
 			ethernet = <&dp2>;
 			phy-mode = "sgmii";
+			status = "okay";
 		};
 	};
 };
